---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Contact Us - ${siteConfig.name} | Editorial Inquiries & Press Office`}
  description="Contact TG Movies and Chief Editor Aman Alria for editorial inquiries, press communications, corrections, feedback, and advertising inquiries."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pb-6 mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 mb-2">
        <span>Direct Communication Channel</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        Contact TG Movies
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-2">
        Get in touch with our editorial desk, film critics, and publisher for inquiries, corrections, or press materials.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-6">
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 font-medium">
        At <strong>TG Movies</strong>, we value direct, open, and responsive communication with our readers, studio partners, PR representatives, and industry contributors. Whether you are providing a verified news tip, requesting a factual correction, pitching an editorial collaboration, or reaching out regarding technical matters, our team is committed to addressing every query promptly and transparently. We believe that credible journalism relies upon accessible lines of communication between editors and the public.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-8 not-prose">
        <!-- Card 1: Primary Editorial Email -->
        <div class="p-6 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-lg shadow-sm">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-sky-100 dark:bg-sky-950/80 flex items-center justify-center text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 8l7.89 5.26a2 2 0 002.22 0L21 8M5 19h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-1">
            Official Editorial Inbox
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mb-3">
            For news submissions, corrections, author communications, and general feedback.
          </p>
          <a href="mailto:amanalha07@gmail.com" class="text-sm font-mono font-bold text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 hover:underline">
            amanalha07@gmail.com
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 2: Editorial Desk -->
        <div class="p-6 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-lg shadow-sm">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-950/80 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M16 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0zM12 14a7 7 0 00-7 7h14a7 7 0 00-7-7z"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-1">
            Chief Editor & Journalist
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mb-3">
            Direct desk of Aman Alria, Chief Editor & Film Journalist.
          </p>
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
            Aman Alria • TG Movies Masthead
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
        Inquiry Categories & Submission Standards
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        To ensure that your correspondence reaches the appropriate editor without delay, we ask correspondents to format their subject headers according to the primary categories detailed below:
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">1. Press Releases, Advance Screeners & Media Access</h3>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        Film production houses, independent distributors, OTT platforms, film festival coordinators, and PR agencies wishing to share advance digital screeners, press kits, official high-resolution posters, casting announcements, or premiere invitations may transmit materials directly to <a href="mailto:amanalha07@gmail.com" class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">amanalha07@gmail.com</a>. Please format the email subject line as <code>[PRESS RELEASE] Film Title - Distributor/Agency</code>. We review all submitted screening materials diligently; however, please note that providing screener access does not guarantee a positive critique or compromise our editorial objectivity.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">2. Factual Corrections, Data Revisions & Retractions</h3>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        Maintaining 100% factual accuracy is our core standard. If you discover a discrepancy in any published box office report, an erroneous release date, a misspelled cast or crew credit, or an outdated streaming license notice, please notify our corrections desk immediately. Subject header: <code>[CORRECTION] Article Title / URL</code>. Please supply verifiable primary source documentation (such as audited trade receipts, distributor press notices, or studio filings). Our senior editorial team investigates every reported error within 24 hours and issues transparent, timestamped updates.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">3. Copyright, DMCA & Intellectual Property Inquiries</h3>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        TG Movies respects the intellectual property rights of filmmakers, studios, and visual artists. All promotional stills, trailers, character names, and movie titles featured across our reviews are utilized strictly under the transformative fair-use doctrine for news reporting, criticism, and educational context. If you are a copyright holder or designated agent and believe that content published on TG Movies infringes your copyright, please dispatch a detailed notice to <a href="mailto:amanalha07@gmail.com" class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">amanalha07@gmail.com</a> with the subject <code>[DMCA NOTICE] Infringement Claim</code> including proof of copyright ownership and specific URL links.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">4. Advertising, Sponsorships & Technical Operations</h3>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        For inquiries regarding programmatic advertising, direct brand sponsorships adhering strictly to Google AdSense compliance policies, syndication licenses, or reporting website bugs (such as layout rendering issues or broken links), please direct your inquiry to our administration team. Please note that we do not sell text-link spam, do not accept sponsored guest posts masquerading as organic news, and do not publish paid favorable reviews.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">5. Reader Feedback & Community Discussions</h3>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        We encourage film lovers and cinephiles to engage directly with our articles through our interactive, Cloudflare-backed discussion section located beneath every review. If you have an in-depth retrospective idea, an essay suggestion, or thoughts on emerging cinema trends, our team welcomes your constructive feedback. You can always share your thoughts directly with Chief Editor Aman Alria via email.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
        Expected Response Timelines & Office Hours
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        Our editorial and digital desk operates Monday through Saturday, 09:00 AM to 07:00 PM Indian Standard Time (IST). While breaking news tips and urgent correction notices are monitored continuously throughout weekends, standard correspondence typically receives a response within 24 to 48 business hours. We thank you for supporting high-integrity independent cinema journalism at TG Movies.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
